=== 1: SIGINT ends the command an interactive shell is running
status: signal 2
bash-n: 0

=== 2: Programs inherit an ignored SIGINT after the shell first waits for one
status: 0
bash-n: 0
--- stdout
|done-4
--- stderr
|bash: cannot set terminal process group (-1): Inappropriate ioctl for device
|bash: no job control in this shell
|#send:Enter
|#expect-prompt
|<INT $$; touch survived.txt'; echo "done-$((2 + 2))"
|#send:Enter
|#expect:done-4
|#expect-prompt
|#send:Ctrl+D
|exit
--- file survived.txt

