=== 13: PROMPT_COMMAND as an associative array is ignored
status: 0
bash-n: 0
--- stdout
|command-ran
--- stderr
|bash: cannot set terminal process group (-1): Inappropriate ioctl for device
|bash: no job control in this shell
|test$ declare -A PROMPT_COMMAND
|test$ PROMPT_COMMAND[x]='echo ASSOC-X'
|test$ PROMPT_COMMAND[y]='echo ASSOC-Y'
|test$ echo command-ran
|test$ unset PROMPT_COMMAND
|test$ exit

=== 14: return does not exit the shell, from PROMPT_COMMAND or the prompt
status: 0
bash-n: 0
--- stdout
|PC-A
|PC-B
|STILL-ALIVE
|PC-A
|PC-B
|STILL-ALIVE-AFTER-BARE-RETURN
--- stderr
|bash: cannot set terminal process group (-1): Inappropriate ioctl for device
|bash: no job control in this shell
|test$ PROMPT_COMMAND=('echo PC-A' 'return' 'echo PC-B')
|bash: return: can only `return' from a function or sourced script
|test$ echo STILL-ALIVE
|bash: return: can only `return' from a function or sourced script
|test$ unset PROMPT_COMMAND
|test$ return
|bash: return: can only `return' from a function or sourced script
|test$ echo STILL-ALIVE-AFTER-BARE-RETURN
|test$ exit

